📍 Level 2: Statistical Modeling & Advanced AnalyticsLevel 2 moves beyond exploratory analysis into the world of inferential statistics and machine learning. 

This phase involves building mathematical models to predict continuous values, analyze temporal trends, and group data points into meaningful segments.

🛠️ Task BreakdownTask 1: Regression AnalysisDataset: Boston House Prices

Objective: Predict the median value of owner-occupied homes based on neighborhood and housing characteristics.

Key Actions:Performed Feature Selection to identify the strongest predictors (e.g., number of rooms vs. crime rate).

Built a Multiple Linear Regression model to quantify the impact of specific variables on property value.
Evaluated model performance using R-squared and Mean Squared Error (MSE).

Tools: Python (Scikit-Learn, NumPy).

Task 2: Time Series AnalysisDataset: Apple Inc. (AAPL) Historical Stock Prices

Objective: Analyze stock market trends and seasonality to understand price movements over time.

Key Actions:Performed Rolling Window Analysis (Moving Averages) to smooth out short-term fluctuations.
Conducted a Stationarity Test (Augmented Dickey-Fuller) to prepare the data for forecasting.
Visualized price trends and volume spikes to identify historical market volatility.

Tools: Python (Pandas, Matplotlib, Statsmodels).

Task 3: Clustering Analysis (K-Means)Dataset: Telecom Customer Churn

Objective: Use unsupervised learning to segment customers into distinct groups based on usage behavior and risk profile.

Key Actions:Applied the Elbow Method to determine the optimal number of clusters ($K$).
Segmented customers based on Total Charges, Service Calls, and Account Length.
Identified a "High-Risk/High-Value" cluster that requires immediate retention focus.

Tools: Python (Scikit-Learn, Seaborn).

📈 Level 2 OutcomesPredictive Accuracy: Developed the ability to model and predict continuous numerical targets (Regression).

Trend Forecasting: Mastered the handling of time-dependent data and financial volatility (Time Series).

Strategic Segmentation: Successfully grouped over 3,000 customers into actionable business segments (Clustering).
